d or partially-written file at the real path because there is no write-to-temp-then-rename step.'"},{"packet":"M7","issue":"F16 honest isPluggedIn fix has no stated RED test.","severity":"medium","evidence":"Plan line 92: 'M7 — F16: honest isPluggedIn via real power-source query (IOKit IOPSCopyPowerSourcesInfo) or nil, not battery == 100. InferenceTelemetry.swift (~:57).' No RED clause.","suggested_edit":"Add: 'RED: with a mocked/injectable power-source query returning \"on battery, 100% charge,\" assert `isPluggedIn` reports `false`/`nil`, not `true` — today the code infers plugged-in from `battery == 100`, which is wrong for a fully-charged unplugged MacBook.'"},{"packet":"M8a,M8b","issue":"Neither F24 (TimeoutConfig honored) nor F25 (privacy: .private logging) has a stated RED test.","severity":"medium","evidence":"Plan line 94: 'M8a — F24: timeout errors read TimeoutConfig instead of hardcoded 300... M8b — F25: transcript-length log → privacy: .private...' No RED clause for either.","suggested_edit":"M8a — 'RED: construct WhisperKitPlugin/WhisperKitProPlugin with a non-default TimeoutConfig value; assert the timeout error/behavior uses that value, not the hardcoded 300.' M8b — 'RED (source-inspection acceptable here, it is a logging-attribute check not a behavior check): assert the transcript-length OSLog call site uses `privacy: .private` in its interpolation.'"},{"packet":"P2","issue":"F17's extraction of a shared ~140-line streaming loop (merging two duplicated code paths) has no verification step at all — not even a directive to confirm existing tests for both overloads still pass post-extraction — despite real regression risk if the two originals subtly differed.","severity":"medium","evidence":"Plan line 100: 'P2 — F17: extract the shared ~140-line streaming loop from the two transcribeStream overloads in StreamingTranscriptionUseCase.swift (keep dropped-yield logging in both).' No RED/verify clause, unlike sibling packet P1 in the same wave which states 'RED: non-UserFacingError throw → error surfaced, not empty results.'","suggested_edit":"Add: 'Verify first: diff the two overloads bodies line-by-line to confirm they are behaviorally identical before merging (not just structurally similar). RED/gate: enumerate the existing StreamingTranscriptionUseCase tests covering both overloads; all must pass unchanged before and after the extraction — if the two overloads currently diverge in any behavior, reconcile that divergence explicitly (do not silently pick one) before merging.'"},{"packet":"P3","issue":"The primary bug fix in this packet (empty rawResponse debug dump) has no stated RED test — only the unrelated dead-code deletion sub-task has a verify step.","severity":"medium","evidence":"Plan line 102: 'P3 — F20 + #224 (Record-Pro): fix PipelineRunner.swift:261–266 empty rawResponse debug dump (capture the real failed response or delete the path); delete dead mergeSpeakers at PipelineRunner.swift:276 (verify zero callers first — issue said 3 copies, only 1 remains).' The 'verify zero callers first' clause covers only the deletion; the rawResponse fix itself has no test description.","suggested_edit":"Add: 'RED: trigger a failed pipeline response through PipelineRunner; assert the debug dump captures the actual non-empty response body/string rather than an empty placeholder — currently the variable feeding the dump is never populated so it always logs empty.'"},{"packet":"A5","issue":"A5's source-inspection RED test doesn't specify how many call sites or which specific failure-path locations must invoke abortRouteChange, so it can pass with the call wired at only one of the three named failure paths while the other two still leak the observer/engine.","severity":"medium","evidence":"Plan line 67: '...Replace those failure paths with abortRouteChange(with:) calls. RED: source-inspection test that failure paths call it.' The prose earlier in the same packet explicitly names three distinct failure paths in handleConfigurationChange() that currently skip cleanup, but the RED spec only says 'failure paths call it' (singular check), not 'each of the three does.'","suggested_edit":"Change to: 'RED: source-inspection test asserting exactly 3 call sites of `abortRouteChange(` appear within handleConfigurationChange()'s three failure branches (one per documented failure path) — not merely that the substring appears once anywhere in the file.'"},{"packet":"A3,A4","issue":"Both packets describe straightforwardly testable behavior fixes (honest duration reporting; no orphaned WAV on failed start) but state no RED test, unlike neighboring A1/A5/A6 in the same wave.","severity":"medium","evidence":"Plan lines 62 and 64 both end with a code-location note but no 'RED:' clause: A3 — 'stop() duration from wavWriter.totalSamplesWritten, not wall clock... Remove try? ... ?? 0 / ?? Date() silent fallbacks (DPS-204).' A4 — 'create WAVWriter inside the do block so failed starts don't orphan 44-byte WAVs.'","suggested_edit":"A3 — 'RED: stop a capture after writing N known samples at rate R; assert reported duration == N/R (derived from samples written), not wall-clock elapsed time, and assert no `try?`/`?? 0` masks a real duration-computation failure.' A4 — 'RED: force converter/tap construction to throw immediately after WAVWriter creation (simulate a failed start); assert no orphaned 44-byte WAV file remains on disk afterward.'"},{"packet":"A7","issue":"No stated RED test, and the fix type (converting fixed-sleep tests to ContinuousClock-based polling) doesn't map cleanly onto the plan's mandatory RED/GREEN TDD rule with no carve-out for pure test-infrastructure refactors.","severity":"low","evidence":"Plan line 73: 'A7 — #198 remainder: fixed sleeps → polling... Build the F9 waitForEvent(in:timeout:) deadline helper (ContinuousClock) once per package; the isArmed polling pattern from Phase 0 is the model.' No RED clause, and the packet is itself a test-suite modification, so the plan's own ground rule ('failing test first, confirm failure via swift test --filter, then implement') has no obvious referent — what test fails before this fix?","suggested_edit":"Add: 'RED: demonstrate the current fixed-sleep test is a source of flakiness/timing-fragility (e.g., temporarily shorten the sleep constant and show the test now fails or races); confirm the polling replacement passes reliably across repeated runs (e.g., `swift test --filter <name> --repeat 20`) without needing the artificial shortening to fail.'"},{"packet":"C3","issue":"The plan's C3 line states no RED test, and issue #213's suggested verification ('verify that ExportTranscriptUseCase and QueryContextUseCase actually filter correctly') is vague about what assertion constitutes 'correctly,' while the real gap (production wiring) is not covered by any existing test.","severity":"medium","evidence":"Plan line 123: 'C3 — #213 PrivacyModeProvider: 11 consumers get nil → wire a real provider at the composition root (default PrivacyMode.default).' No RED clause. tokensave_search confirms `MockPrivacyModeProvider` test doubles already exist (`Record-App/Tests/Unit/Business/Mocks/MockPrivacyModeProvider.swift`, `Record-ML/Tests/Unit/Mocks/MockPrivacyModeProvider.swift`) and `QueryContextUseCaseTests.swift` already has privacy-mode-aware tests (e.g. `alwaysModeBlocksAll`) — but these only exercise use-case logic when a provider IS injected; none of them test that `AppAssemblerBuilders` actually constructs and injects a real, non-nil provider in production, which is the actual defect per the issue.","suggested_edit":"Add: 'RED: add a composition-root-level test asserting AppAssemblerBuilders constructs a non-nil PrivacyModeProvider and passes it into all 11 named consumers — today every consumer receives nil by default; the existing MockPrivacyModeProvider-based use-case tests validate logic only when a provider is manually supplied and do not exercise production wiring.'"},{"packet":"C1","issue":"Issue #211's suggested 'Add tests' step (verify guard thresholds via MockDiskSpaceMonitor) is already implemented and already passing, so it is not a valid RED gate for this packet; the actual missing behavior — a real DiskSpaceMonitor conformance and its production wiring — has no test specified anywhere.","severity":"low","evidence":"gh issue view 211 says: '3. Add tests — verify the guard thresholds (100 MB block, 500 MB warn) using MockDiskSpaceMonitor.' tokensave_search shows these tests already exist and presumably pass: `Record-Presentation/Tests/Unit/Presentation/RecordingStateViewModelTests.swift:190` `hardBlockThresholdIs100MB` and `:196` `lowDiskWarningThresholdIs500MB`. Grep of `Record-App/Sources/TheRecord/*.swift` confirms zero references to DiskSpaceMonitor today, so production wiring genuinely is missing (issue is accurate there) — but the plan/issue's stated test won't go RED before this fix and won't distinguish fixed from unfixed, since it already tests only the ViewModel-side guard logic with a manually-supplied mock.","suggested_edit":"Add to C1: 'RED: add a test asserting AppAssemblerBuilders passes a non-nil DiskSpaceMonitor into the constructed RecordingStateViewModel/SettingsViewModel (the existing MockDiskSpaceMonitor threshold tests already pass and do not exercise this); optionally, a focused unit test for the new FileSystemDiskSpaceMonitor.availableBytes() returning a plausible non-zero value against a real/temp URL.'"}]}}
